\fs96 \cf2 GPU programming fundamentals\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 This guide explores the fundamentals of GPU programming using the Mojo programming language, covering essential concepts and techniques for developing GPU-accelerated applications that can work on a variety of supported GPUs from different vendors.\
Key topics covered in this guide:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Understanding the CPU-GPU programming model.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Working with Mojo's GPU support through the standard library.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Managing GPU devices and contexts using 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 DeviceContext
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 .\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Writing and executing kernel functions for parallel computation.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Memory management and data transfer between CPU and GPU.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Organizing threads and thread blocks for optimal performance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Before diving into GPU programming, ensure you have a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/requirements/#gpu-compatibility"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 compatible GPU}} and the necessary development environment installed. And if you're new to GPU programming, we suggest you read the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/gpu/architecture/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 Intro to GPU architectures}}.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 Overview of GPU programming in Mojo\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The Mojo language, including its standard library and open source MAX kernels library, allow you to develop GPU-enabled applications.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 GPU support in the Mojo standard library\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul \ulc5 gpu}} package of the Mojo standard library includes several subpackages for interacting with GPUs, with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/gpu/host/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul \ulc5 gpu.host}} package providing most of the commonly used APIs. However, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/sys/info/"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \ul \ulc5 sys}} package contains a few basic introspection functions for determining whether a system has a supported GPU:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/sys/info/has_accelerator/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul has_accelerator()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Returns 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  if the host system has an accelerator and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 False
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  otherwise.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/sys/info/has_amd_gpu_accelerator/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul has_amd_gpu_accelerator()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Returns 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  if the host system has an AMD GPU and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 False
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  otherwise.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/sys/info/has_apple_gpu_accelerator/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul has_apple_gpu_accelerator()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Returns 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  if the host system has an Apple silicon GPU and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 False
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  otherwise.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs28 \cf5 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/std/sys/info/has_nvidia_gpu_accelerator/"}}{\fldrslt \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\ul has_nvidia_gpu_accelerator()}}
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
: Returns 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 True
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  if the host system has an NVIDIA GPU and 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 False
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  otherwise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 These functions are useful for conditional compilation or execution depending on whether a supported GPU is available.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

